hus|n|A solid body which may be generated by the rotation of a parallelogram round one its sides; or a body of rollerlike form, of which the longitudinal section is oblong, and the cross section is circular. ; The space inclosed by any cylindrical surface. The space may be limited or unlimited in length. ; Any hollow body of cylindrical form ; The chamber of a steam engine in which the piston is moved by the force of steam. ; The barrel of an air or other pump. ; The revolving platen or bed which produces the impression or carries the type in a cylinder press. ; The bore of a gun; the turning chambered breech of a revolver. ; The revolving square prism carrying the cards in a Jacquard loom.	a:yxm,73,10;1wdg,48,11;165t,41,5;1x3f,27,5;165q,26,3;1mx7,1,1~1wdg,48,11;yxm,73,10;1x3f,27,5;165t,41,5;165q,26,3;1mx7,1,1	v:1mx7,1,1~1mx7,1,1	n:yxm,56,3;k8y,40,6;21bo,13,2;1bbk,11,4~k8y,40,6;1bbk,11,4;yxm,56,3;21bo,13,2	N:1vm5,45,4;k8y,37,5;29v0,28,2;1egg,22,2~k8y,37,5;1vm5,45,4;1egg,22,2;29v0,28,2
